00:26:15.441 --> 00:26:20.904
From Microsoft Developer Blogs: Is “sort by impact” just vibes?

00:26:21.009 --> 00:26:26.931
“Give me the top five, sorted by impact.” People ask AI agents for this

00:26:26.931 --> 00:26:32.390
all the time, whether it’s a backlog or a pile of growth ideas. Yet “

00:26:32.390 --> 00:26:37.140
impact” is one of the vaguest words in the language. It could mean how

00:26:37.140 --> 00:26:41.348
many users benefit, how much money comes in or how much you get for

00:26:41.348 --> 00:26:47.445
the effort. Hardly anyone says which, so we suspected the order agents come back

00:26:47.445 --> 00:26:54.070
with is just vibes. It looks plausible, but there’s nothing behind it. We were

00:26:54.070 --> 00:27:01.654
wrong, though not in a reassuring way. Across 1,500 runs with four models, agents

00:27:01.654 --> 00:27:06.417
ranked the same list in nearly the same order every time, and different models

00:27:06.417 --> 00:27:09.072
largely agreed with each other.

