Shop for you to pick from.

00:27:59.529 --> 00:28:01.320
Python.

00:28:01.425 --> 00:28:05.856
From Real Python: Conditional Statements in Python.

00:28:05.961 --> 00:28:10.086
From the previous tutorials in this series, you now have quite a bit of

00:28:10.086 --> 00:28:15.592
Python code under your belt. Everything you have seen so far has consisted of

00:28:15.592 --> 00:28:21.981
sequential execution, in which statements are always performed one after the next, in exactly

00:28:21.981 --> 00:28:29.203
the order specified. But the world is often more complicated than that. Frequently, a

00:28:29.203 --> 00:28:35.369
program needs to skip over some statements, execute a series of statements repetitively, or

00:28:35.369 --> 00:28:41.550
choose between alternate sets of statements to execute. That is where control structures come

00:28:41.550 --> 00:28:46.911
in. A control structure directs the order of execution of the statements in a

00:28:46.911 --> 00:28:51.360
program (referred to as the program’s control flow).

